# Flutter web hot reload after edits

The Flutter Chrome app is started by the agent via `frontend/tool/run_chrome.ps1` (stdin is redirected). Do not ask the user to restart `flutter run`.

After any Dart/UI/theme/asset change under `frontend/`:

1. Finish the file edits.
2. Run `frontend/tool/reload.ps1 -Key r` for widget/logic/text changes (hot reload).
3. Run `frontend/tool/reload.ps1 -Key R` for `main.dart`, `app_theme.dart`, `pubspec.yaml` assets, or other app-structure changes (hot restart).
4. If that script is not running, start it yourself:

```powershell
# from frontend/
powershell -File tool/run_chrome.ps1
```

Use `--web-port 5555` (the script default). App URL: http://localhost:5555 — keep **one** tab open; do not run `-d chrome` (it always opens a new tab on process start).

Do not tell the user to stop/start Flutter unless the managed process has died. If you must start it, use `tool/run_chrome.ps1` (`web-server`) and refresh the existing tab.
